<title>FRANCE: Rouen grain exports fell to 323,224 tns in August.</title>
<headline>Rouen grain exports fell to 323,224 tns in August.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grain exports from Rouen fell to 323,224 tonnes in August 1996 from 491,000 tonnes in August 1995, port officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The 323,224 tonnes grain total included 314,581 tonnes of wheat and 8,643 tonnes of barley, they said.</p>
<p>Wheat destinations break down as follows (in tonnes)</p>
<p>    West Africa			    9,250</p>
<p>    Bangladesh			    20,000</p>
<p>    Canary Islands			14,700</p>
<p>    Ethiopia				19,000</p>
<p>    Finland				  2,200</p>
<p>    Britain				 17,343</p>
<p>    Greece				   5,500</p>
<p>    Ireland				  3,010</p>
<p>    Italy				  138,178</p>
<p>    Libya				    8,900</p>
<p>    Madagascar			    14,300</p>
<p>    Morocco				 31,880</p>
<p>    Poland				  11,905</p>
<p>    Portugal				 8,250</p>
<p>    Reunion Island			10,165</p>
<p>Barley destinations break down as follows (in tonnes)</p>
<p>    Italy				    1,555</p>
<p>    Reunion Island			 7,088</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +331 42215432</p>
</text>
